Trace every message received from the SEP (ep, type, raw msg0).

The sep.rs stub dispatches only EP_BOOT/EP_DISCOVER and handles the boot ACKs
(0x69/0xD2/0x6A) silently, so we cannot see how far SEP boot gets nor whether
SEPOS sends anything after IMG4. Add one dev_info! in the central
process_message() to log every inbound message. Goal (Touch ID RE, MacFingerprint):
determine where the macOS-26 SEP boot stalls -- do we get the ACKs, does any
advertise (ep 0xFD) or unknown message arrive afterwards?

--- a/drivers/soc/apple/sep.rs
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/sep.rs
@@ -254,6 +254,13 @@
     }
